# Lean Verification

Verification burns credits. Default to the cheapest check that catches real errors, then stop.

## Do

- Rely on TypeScript/linter errors surfaced after edits as the primary check
- Run at most ONE `tsc --noEmit` or build check per task, and only for non-trivial changes
- Trust that a correct code change works; hand visual/UI confirmation back to the user ("reload the page and check X")

## Don't

- Don't open the browser, take screenshots, or snapshot pages to verify UI changes unless the user explicitly asks
- Don't curl pages repeatedly to confirm rendered HTML matches an edit
- Don't restart or touch dev servers to force recompiles just to verify — report the suspected stale-server issue and let the user decide
- Don't re-verify something already confirmed once

If a check fails in a way that suggests stale tooling (dev server not picking up changes), say so and stop instead of investigating with more commands.
